  <title>7.4.0: Lesson Overview</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01793</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.4.0: Lesson Overview</md:title>
    <md:uuid>f9474c1e-45ac-413f-993a-74e190b4511f</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <para id="para-00001">In this lesson, you will investigate how quantities that grow quadratically compare to those that grow exponentially. You will use different mathematical models to show the relationship between the functions to determine which one grows faster.</para>
      <para id="para-00002">When you finish this lesson, you will be able to:</para>
      <list id="list-00001">
        <item>Explain using graphs, tables, or calculations how exponential functions eventually grow faster than quadratic functions.</item>
      </list>
      <para id="para-00003">Here are the <emphasis>activities</emphasis> that will help you reach those goals:</para>
      <list id="list-00002">
        <item>7.4.1: Comparing Expressions</item>
        <item>7.4.2: Exploring Linear, Exponential, and Quadratic Growth <list id="list-00003">
            <item>7.4.2: Self Check</item>
            <item>7.4.2: Additional Resources</item>
          </list></item>
        <item>7.4.3: Comparing Exponential and Quadratic Functions <list id="list-00004">
            <item>7.4.3: Self Check</item>
            <item>7.4.3: Additional Resources</item>
          </list></item>
        <item>7.4.4: Comparing Exponential and Quadratic Expressions</item>
      </list>
      <para id="para-00004">After that, you’ll <emphasis>practice and review</emphasis>.</para>
      <list id="list-00005">
        <item>7.4.5: Practice</item>
        <item>7.4.6: Lesson Summary</item>
      </list>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>